  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "This week (01 - 05 June) witnessed the largest Posidonia 2026 International Shipping Exhibition in Athens, \nGreece, in the event's nearly 60-year history. The city was energized by a dynamic atmosphere, combining \nglobal trade discussions with events, conferences, sports competitions, and seaside celebrations all over the \nAthens Riviera. The event drew over 40,000 participants, shifting focus away from S+P transactions and \nmoving towards building and enhancing networking opportunities.",
    "bulkers": "Despite the \"Posidonia lull\", asset values stayed robust at historically high levels, supported \nby long-term positive outlooks and a limited availability of modern vessels for sale. This week, we \nrecorded a total of 15 transactions, comprising 2 Capesize, 5 Kamsarmax, 2 Supramax, and 6 \nHandysize bulk carriers. Several of these deals established new price benchmarks. For a more detailed \nreview and additional information regarding these transactions, kindly refer to our \"representative \nsales\" section.",
    "demolition": "The Subcontinent markets remain same as last week with minimal activity. For an \noverview of demolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
